<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  fleet-rebase — the comment gesture for rebasing a stale pull request (plan 0115).
  Every 120s, reads the owner's `rebase` comments on open pull requests and, when
  every check passes, rebases the branch onto main and pushes it so CI runs again
  on the new head. Replies on the pull request either way. docs/rebase.md has the
  refusals and what to do instead.

  NOT INSTALLED BY THE PLAN THAT SHIPS IT. The owner installs it (opshost):
    mkdir -p ~/dev/.fleet
    cp launchd/org.eunomia.fleet-rebase.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/org.eunomia.fleet-rebase.plist
  Verify before trusting it: run it by hand once as the sweep in dry-run mode (the
  dry-run flag of bin/fleet-rebase), with the same environment as below, and confirm the first line names a repository count
  (for example "sweeping 1 repositories"). It pushes nothing and posts nothing.

  ENVIRONMENT. This copies fleet-stalled's shape but NOT its environment, which
  sets only a notify URL. FLEET_OPERATOR_UID is required:
  empty, the sweep exits non-zero and names the variable, instead of becoming a
  silent no-op that looks installed. Its value MUST MATCH the installed
  org.eunomia.fleet-watch.plist's, which is the one the `respawn` comment already
  uses. The repository list is config/repos.conf (plan 0134), no variable. FLEET_FORGEJO_URL must match it too. The author-role
  token helper is FLEET_AUTHOR_TOKEN_CMD; fleet-watch.plist sets none, so it is
  empty here and the default helper is used. If that file ever sets one, copy it.

  SSH. The push goes over ssh, so this unit must be able to reach the ssh agent:
  the same constraint bin/orchestrator's _ENV_ALLOW comment documents for
  SSH_AUTH_SOCK. A launchd job does not inherit the login session's socket; if
  the first real push fails with a permission error, that is the cause.

  RUNS FROM THE PINNED WORKTREE, not ~/dev/eunomia — the shared clone sits on
  whatever branch a session last left it on. The pin is a detached worktree of
  this repo at ~/.local/share/pins/eunomia; fleet-watch reports when it falls
  behind. The verb itself works only in a fresh temporary clone.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>org.eunomia.fleet-rebase</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/operator/.local/share/pins/eunomia/bin/fleet-rebase</string>
    <string>--sweep</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <!-- the sweep's repositories are config/repos.conf's `dispatch` lines (plan 0134) -->
    <!-- numeric Forgejo user id of the owner; must match fleet-watch.plist -->
    <key>FLEET_OPERATOR_UID</key><string></string>
    <key>FLEET_FORGEJO_URL</key><string>http://forge.example:3000</string>
    <!-- empty = the default author-role helper; see ENVIRONMENT above -->
    <key>FLEET_AUTHOR_TOKEN_CMD</key><string></string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>120</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>Nice</key><integer>5</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/rebase.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/operator/dev/.fleet/rebase.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
